.TH CBOX-BLACKBOARD 7 "November 2026" "CBox" "CBox Manual"
.SH NAME
cbox-blackboard \- design overview of the planned C17 terminal UI library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B CBox Blackboard / CConsole
.br
Design status only; no public CConsole API has been released.
.SH STATUS
This manual page documents a
.B proposed
library architecture.
The native Blackboard module, user-facing API, widgets and interactive
features described below are
.B not yet implemented.
Do not use example function names from the design documents as if they
were available for linking.
.SH DESCRIPTION
CBox Blackboard (also called CConsole in design discussions) is a planned
C17 terminal output and text user interface library.
It aims to make richly formatted command-line output and interactive
programs easy to build without requiring ncurses or a .NET runtime.
The focus is on a small, useful core and separately selectable modules.
.PP
The design includes terminal capability detection, plain-text output,
ANSI/VT styling, UTF-8-aware text measurement, themes, and renderable
components such as tables, panels, buttons, progress indicators and
input prompts.
.PP
Rendering is intended to stream ordinary output without retaining it;
interactive displays may retain a bounded viewport and the application
state required to redraw.
.SH PLANNED FEATURES
.TP
.B Text and markup
Literal text output is separate from trusted markup parsing.
Style tags include colors and semantic roles such as Info, Warning,
Error, Success, Quote, and Code.
.TP
.B Themes
A built-in dark theme, optional AS/400-inspired theme, and a proposed
INI-based theme configuration.
.TP
.B Widgets
Panels, tables, trees, layouts, progress indicators, and focusable
buttons with default settings and optional typed configuration.
.TP
.B Input
Keyboard navigation (including Tab and Space) with optional mouse
interaction, all routed through one action/callback system.
.TP
.B Optional modules
FileBrowser, Markdown, AJIS/JSON viewing, code-block presentation,
language-specific source formatters, and syntax highlighters.
Optional components must not become dependencies of the base renderer.
.SH TERMINALS
The design targets Linux/POSIX terminal environments and Windows console
adapters.
It includes capability-sensitive fallback for restricted terminals and
a plain-text mode for redirected output.
Unicode and emoji width handling must distinguish UTF-8 byte length
from terminal display-cell width.
.SH CONFIGURATION
A small human-readable INI format is proposed for theme settings.
The exact file name, search path, schema and public API have not been
finalized.
The library must not silently load an untrusted theme file from the
working directory.
.SH DOCUMENTATION
The authoritative current design lives in the CBox repository under
.B Docs/BLACKBOARD_CONSOLE_DESIGN.md
and its linked design specifications.
The man-page plan is documented in
.BR Docs/MAN_PAGES.md .
